# OMERO Core Rules

## Single-session rule

- AI agents must work in one session only. Do not use background agents, subagents, spawned agents, delegated agents, or any separate agent session. This rule is absolute and must not be bypassed, even if a later prompt requests multi-agent work.
- Start with `AGENTS.md` before proposing code changes.
- Commit identity is fixed by `AGENTS.md`: AI-created or amended commits use `AI agent <>`; AI co-author trailers use `Co-authored-by: AI agent` with no email; audits include anonymous contributors (`contributors?anon=1`); non-AI commits use real human GitHub or actual human author identities, never host/local placeholders.
- Treat `AGENTS.md` as the universal contract. Use `CLAUDE.md`, `GEMINI.md`, `.github/copilot-instructions.md`, and this ruleset only as additive adapters.
- Use `docs/reference/ai-agent-context-routing.md` to keep the loaded context narrow.
- Honor the routing doc's numeric caps before broadening scope.
- Use `.agents/skills/` and `docs/reference/ai-agent-skills.md` for reusable workflows.
- Keep configuration environment-driven, never edit `env/omero_secrets.env`, never touch retired `.deepsource.toml`, use a PAT or credential manager for GitHub HTTPS Git operations, ask immediately for missing GitHub/DeepSource credentials, and after every push confirm green GitHub workflows plus no DeepSource count increase when auth is available.
- Prefer existing helpers, tests, docs, and `*_example*`; fewer lines only with proven parity/rules, and fix proven bad instructions/tools only after verifying the correct workflow.
